---
description: >
  Correct Locations for Cursor Rules
  
  When creating or modifying Cursor rules, you MUST put them in the correct location based on their scope:
  
  Agent-specific rules → agents/.cursor/rules/ (Python, Temporal workflows, tools)
  Backend-specific rules → back-end/.cursor/rules/ (TypeScript, Express, Prisma)
  Frontend-specific rules → front-end/.cursor/rules/ (React, TypeScript, UI components)
  Project-wide rules → .cursor/rules/ (git, general practices, workflow rules)
  
  NEVER use .cursorrules/ - it is not read by Cursor!
  
  All rule files must have .mdc extension and include frontmatter with description.
  
  Project-wide workflow rules (always applied):
  - process.mdc - Orchestrates when to use Research → Plan → Implement workflow
  - research.mdc - Guidelines for researching the codebase before changes
  - plan.mdc - Guidelines for creating detailed implementation plans
  - implement.mdc - Guidelines for implementing changes following approved plans
apply:
  when: always
---
